<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Machares</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 65 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Machares was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates VI of Pontus</a> who governed the Bosporan Kingdom as his father's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-mithridatic-war">Third Mithridatic War</a> he made peace with the Roman general Lucullus in 70 BCE and sent him supplies. When Mithridates arrived in the Bosporus in 65 BCE after his defeat, Machares fled and died, by his own hand according to most accounts.</p></div>
